{"title":"20 Favorite Books from 20 Years of The Marginalian","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/10/24/20-books/","date":1792892772000,"content":"<p>It is a beautiful dream, that there is something out there to instruct you how to live — a secret handed down by your parents or your teachers, a system like liberal arts education or cognitive behavioral therapy, a slogan held up by your heroes declaring the answer to the bottomless question of why you are here. </p>\n<p>Whenever you wake up, however you wake up, you find yourself on a path no one else can walk for you, a path you must make by walking. Still, you can find signposts that keep you from losing your way in loneliness. “You think your pain and your heartbreak are unprecedented in the history of the world,” James Baldwin <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2017/05/24/james-baldwin-life-magazine-1963/\">wrote</a>, “but then you read.” </p>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/qKd8UMjQ2Mo\" target=\"_blank\">celebrating twenty years of <em>The Marginalian</em></a> — this ongoing record of learning how to live written in marginalia on the books I have read — I have attempted the impossible: to distill a lifetime of reading into the twenty books that have served as the most enduring signposts, apart from <a href=\"https://themarginalian.org/books\">those I have written</a> (which always both shape and are shaped by a writer’s life more profoundly than any books read). Here they are, in no particular order.</p>\n<h5>LEAVES OF GRASS (WALT WHITMAN)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/04/18/whitman-traversal/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/leavesofgrass_margaretcook.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/04/18/whitman-traversal/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>A RESPONSIBILITY TO AWE (REBECCA ELSON)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Responsibility-Awe-Poems-Oxford-Poets/dp/1903039541/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i2.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/aresponsibilitytoawe.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/02/24/dark-matter/\">Some</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2020/04/10/antidotes-to-fear-of-death-rebecca-elson/\">of</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/07/11/stephon-alexander-rebecca-elson-explaining-relativity/\">why</a> I love it</em></p>\n<h5>EINSTEIN’S DREAMS (ALAN LIGHTMAN)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Einsteins-Dreams-Alan-Lightman/dp/140007780X/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/einsteinsdreams_lightman.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/08/28/alan-lightman-einsteins-dreams/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THE LOG FROM THE SEA OF CORTEZ (JOHN STEINBECK)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Log-Sea-Cortez-Penguin-Classics/dp/0140187448/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/steinbeck_seaofcortez.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/11/09/steinbeck-log-from-the-sea-of-cortez/\">Why I love it</a></em></p>\n<h5>THE ABUNDANCE (ANNIE DILLARD)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Abundance-Narrative-Essays-Old-New/dp/0062432974/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/anniedillard_abundance.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/10/14/annie-dillard-weasel/\">Some</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2017/08/01/annie-dillard-total-solar-eclipse/\">of</a> why I love it</em></p>\n<h5>THE RIVER OF CONSCIOUSNESS (OLIVER SACKS)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/River-Consciousness-Oliver-Sacks/dp/0385352565/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/riverofconsciousness_sacks.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2017/11/09/oliver-sacks-the-river-of-consciousness-the-creative-self/\">Some</a> of why I love it</em></p>\n<h5>THE BOOK OF DELIGHTS (ROSS GAY)\t</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Book-Delights-Essays-Ross-Gay/dp/1616207922/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/bookofdelights_rossgay.jpg?resize=768%2C1088&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/12/01/ross-gay-book-of-delights/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>WILLARD GIBBS (MURIEL RUKEYSER)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Willard-Gibbs-Whole-Simpler-Parts/dp/1961341158/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Gibbs.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/04/24/muriel-rukeyser-willard-gibbs/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THE DICTIONARY OF OBSCURE SORROWS (JOHN KOENIG)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Dictionary-Obscure-Sorrows-John-Koenig/dp/1501153641/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/obscuresorrows.jpg?resize=768%2C1080&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2024/04/12/dictionary-of-obscure-sorrows/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THE FRAGILE SPECIES (LEWIS THOMAS)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fragile-Species-Lewis-Thomas/dp/0684843021/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/thefragilespecies_lewisthomas.jpg?resize=768%2C1157&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/03/02/the-fragile-species-lewis-thomas/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THE SOURCE OF SELF-REGARD (TONI MORRISON)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Source-Self-Regard-Selected-Speeches-Meditations/dp/0525521038/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/thesourceofself-regard_morrison.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/03/06/the-source-of-self-regard-toni-morrison-wisdom-information/\">Some</a> <a>of</a> why I love it</em></p>\n<h5>THE STAR THROWER (LOREN EISELEY)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Star-Thrower-Loren-Eiseley/dp/0156849097/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/thestarthrower_eiseley.jpg?w=674&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2024/02/03/loren-eiseley-birds/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>EXISTENTIALISTS AND MYSTICS (IRIS MURDOCH)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Existentialists-Mystics-Writings-Philosophy-Literature/dp/0140264922/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/irismurdoch_existentialistsandmystics.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/01/08/iris-murdoch-the-sublime-and-the-good/\">Some</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/06/23/iris-murdoch-the-sea-the-sea/\">of</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/10/21/iris-murdoch-unselfing/\">why</a> I love it</em></p>\n<h5>UPSTREAM (MARY OLIVER)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Upstream-Selected-Essays-Mary-Oliver/dp/1594206708/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/maryoliver_upstream.jpg?w=468&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/10/12/mary-oliver-upstream-creativity-power-time/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>CHAOS (JAMES GLEICK)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Chaos-Making-Science-James-Gleick/dp/0749386061/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/jamesgleick_chaos.jpg?resize=768%2C1166&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/02/22/mandelbrot-fractals-chaos/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THE WAVE IN THE MIND (URSULA K. LE GUIN)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Wave-Mind-Essays-Writer-Imagination/dp/1590300068/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/leguin_waveinthemind.jpg?w=680&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/10/22/telling-is-listening-ursula-k-le-guin-communication/\">Some of</a> why I love it</em></p>\n<h5>NOTHING PERSONAL (JAMES BALDWIN)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Richard-Avedon-James-Baldwin-Personal/dp/3836569531/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/avedonbaldwin_nothingpersonal.jpg?resize=768%2C1018&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2020/04/23/james-baldwin-nothing-personal-4-am/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>THANKS (RACHEL HÉBERT)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://acornpressoakland.com/products/the-book-of-thanks\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/hebert_thanks1.jpg?w=421&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/11/16/rachel-hebert-thanks/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>CONSOLATIONS (DAVID WHYTE)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Consolations-Nourishment-Underlying-Meaning-Everyday/dp/1786897636/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/davidwhyte_consolations.jpg?resize=768%2C1215&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<em><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/04/29/david-whyte-consolations-words/\">Some</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/05/15/david-whyte-consolations-anger-forgiveness-maturity/\">of</a> <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/04/11/david-whyte-vulnerability/\">why</a> I love it</em></p>\n<h5>A MADMAN DREAMS OF TURING MACHINES (JANNA LEVIN)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Madman-Dreams-Turing-Machines/dp/1400032407/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/madman_levin.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/09/20/janna-levin-a-madman-dreams-of-turing-machines/\"><em>Why I love it</em></a></p>\n<h5>(AND SOME FROM ME)</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/traversal/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/traversal_cover.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/figuring/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/figuring_jacket_final.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/uiv-book/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/UiV_book_cover.jpg\" width=\"325\" /></a></p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"953337b0107d1e7ac2c07a72e2b47a58e0f88c3183fd43fa54123cd2f2ff6729","category":"Sites"}